<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36650" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξᾰλίνδω</span></b> , only aor.
		part.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαλίσας [ῑ</span>], pf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξήλῑκα</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>roll out</i> or <i>thoroughly,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπαγε τὸν ἵππον ἐξαλίσας
			οἴκαδε</span> take him away <i>when you have given</i> him
				<i>a good roll on the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλινδήθρα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				32
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				11.18
			</span></i>); to which Strepsiades retorts, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξήλικας ἐμέ γ᾽ ἐκ τῶν ἐμῶν</span> you <i>have
				rolled</i> me <i>out of</i> house and home, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				33
			</span></i>.</div>
